{#
  Intent Buffer Panel - The Frontallappen (Planning Center)

  OPUS-031 Layer 1.5: Shows what the system PLANS to do next.

  This is the bridge between Intention and Action:
  - AI proposes an intent (set_pending_intent)
  - Human sees it in OPUS.md
  - Human checks "Execute" checkbox to approve
  - System executes the approved intent
  - Result appears in Syscall Console

  THE COGNITIVE LOOP:
  Intention (Buffer) -> Action (Syscall) -> Memory (Console) -> Reflection (Dashboard)

  Required context:
    - pending_intent: Dict with intent details or None
      - intent: str (natural language description)
      - syscall_type: str
      - params: Dict
      - requires_approval: bool
      - approved: bool
      - created_at: str (ISO timestamp)

  Design Decisions (OPUS-031):
    - DD4: Bidirectional Control Surface
    - DD6: Intent before Action (human-in-the-loop)
#}

